#: ../../preface.md:1 44eba5a9fd6544d399d00deea1cc35e1
msgid "Preface"
msgstr "前言"

#: ../../preface.md:3 fc88d38fcee442f9984c5a53f68ef7c9
msgid ""
"Efficiency and productivity analysis lies at the intersection of production "
"economics, operations research, and empirical measurement. Modern software "
"can solve a large DEA program quickly; the harder task is to specify a "
"defensible production technology, choose a measure consistent with the "
"decision problem, and explain what the resulting benchmark does and does not"
" establish. This book is written around that harder task."
msgstr ""
"效率与生产率分析处在生产经济学、运筹学和经验测度的交汇处。现代软件能够迅速求解大型 DEA "
"规划，更难的工作却是设定一套经得起论证的生产技术，选择与决策问题相符的测度，并说明所得标杆结论能够支持什么、又不能证明什么。本书围绕这项更具挑战的工作展开。"

#: ../../preface.md:9 4bf90c7ccd9f436aa47e35d1ea32fea5
msgid ""
"The intended audience includes readers encountering frontier methods for the"
" first time, applied researchers who need a reproducible workflow, and "
"specialists who want a consistent reference across classical, productivity, "
"and environmental DEA. The exposition begins with production plans, "
"technologies, efficiency, and distance functions before introducing "
"individual linear programs. Advanced chapters retain the same notation and "
"distinguish changes in the technology from changes in the measure or "
"reference sample."
msgstr ""
"本书面向三类读者：初次接触前沿方法的学习者、需要可重复研究流程的应用研究者，以及希望在经典 DEA、生产率和环境 DEA "
"之间采用一致参照体系的专业人士。正文先介绍生产方案、生产技术、效率和距离函数，再进入各个线性规划。进阶章节沿用同一套符号，并明确区分生产技术的变化、测度的变化与参照样本的变化。"

#: ../../preface.md:17 d175b5a9c7604dd3a688857f91ce72b1
msgid ""
"A new reader should leave with more than a catalogue of acronyms: the aim is"
" to make it possible to state a performance question in economic terms, "
"choose assumptions that fit the organization, and interpret a score without "
"claiming more than the comparison can support. Applied readers can use the "
"worked cases to move from a defensible study design to targets, "
"decompositions, sensitivity analysis, and reporting. Researchers can use the"
" common notation to compare methods whose historical names sometimes conceal"
" the same idea---or suggest equivalence where an economically important "
"difference remains."
msgstr "初学者读完本书，得到的不应只是一串缩写。我们的目标是帮助读者用经济学语言提出绩效问题，选择符合组织实际的假设，并在不超出比较证据边界的前提下解释得分。应用研究者可以借助完整案例，从可信的研究设计走向目标方案、分解、敏感性分析和结果报告。研究人员则可利用统一符号，比较那些有时因历史名称不同而掩盖同一思想、又有时因名称相近而掩盖重要经济差异的方法。"

#: ../../preface.md:25 e7df1c0e93e74ca68ab1ab71566408f6
msgid "Organization by economic substance"
msgstr "按经济实质组织内容"

#: ../../preface.md:27 00ff15423c6b406e980c92a0558582dc
msgid ""
"The DEA literature contains many names for formulations that are "
"mathematically equivalent, as well as similar names for methods that impose "
"different production assumptions. This book organizes the field around the "
"economic question being asked and the assumptions needed to make the "
"comparison meaningful:"
msgstr ""
"DEA "
"文献中，数学上等价的模型常有多个名称，名称相近的方法也可能采用不同的生产假设。本书按照所要回答的经济问题，以及使比较具有意义所需的假设来组织这一领域："

#: ../../preface.md:32 3759f03149d042009d0616b48fe86d5c
msgid "the roles and units of observed variables;"
msgstr "观测变量的角色与计量单位；"

#: ../../preface.md:33 baa043eac506471d9edc0ef60ceaf8b2
msgid "the axioms defining the production technology;"
msgstr "界定生产技术的公理；"

#: ../../preface.md:34 0f01d9c957894ff393554cef483a77c6
msgid "the efficiency or productivity measure;"
msgstr "效率或生产率测度；"

#: ../../preface.md:35 b029698f0b6d4c60946428768a942491
msgid "the reference technology and comparison population;"
msgstr "参照技术与比较总体；"

#: ../../preface.md:36 2e44cfd1134542dbaa810c3f90240fa8
msgid "the internal structure of production;"
msgstr "生产活动的内部结构；"

#: ../../preface.md:37 852b28aab91a42d0ba71849a238f3741
msgid "the inferential and substantive purpose of the analysis."
msgstr "分析的推断目的与实质目的。"

#: ../../preface.md:39 d06497686a5e4d889cab53223c1a0ca8
msgid ""
"Historical names such as CCR and BCC are retained because they connect "
"readers to the literature, but they do not determine the taxonomy. "
"Equivalent multiplier and envelopment formulations are treated together. "
"Methods remain separate when disposability, convexity, returns to scale, "
"direction, or reference technology changes the managerial counterfactual or "
"the economic quantity being measured."
msgstr ""
"本书保留 CCR、BCC "
"等历史名称，以便读者与既有文献衔接，但不以这些名称决定方法分类。等价的乘数形式与包络形式放在一起讲解。当可处置性、凸性、规模报酬、方向或参照技术改变了管理反事实或所测经济量时，相应方法仍会分别讨论。"

#: ../../preface.md:45 12ed355da407473aae622a471e2190f9
msgid ""
"The main text is deliberately DEA-centered rather than a survey of every "
"frontier method. Index-number theory, stochastic frontier analysis, robust "
"nonparametric frontiers, and statistical inference are mentioned where they "
"clarify the scope or limitations of DEA-based conclusions. Appendices "
"synthesize relationships among the principal families; paper-specific "
"extensions and exhaustive implementation details remain in the separate "
"package Documentation."
msgstr ""
"正文有意以 DEA 为中心，而不是穷尽所有前沿方法。指数理论、随机前沿分析、稳健非参数前沿和统计推断，只在有助于说明 DEA "
"结论的范围或局限时引入。附录综合主要方法族之间的关系；针对单篇论文的扩展和详尽的实现细节则留在单独的包文档中。"

#: ../../preface.md:52 520a81c81c2a4ce099d7e07fea3ce2b6
msgid "The book and DEAPack"
msgstr "本书与 DEAPack"

#: ../../preface.md:54 85df246891f6461d9bbbf6a0dc8fad40
msgid ""
"DEAPack is the computational companion to the book, not its organizing "
"subject. A chapter first defines a production problem and develops its "
"theoretical measure. Code then reproduces a claim, reveals the targets or "
"decomposition behind a score, and shows whether the conditions needed to "
"interpret that comparison are satisfied. Complete signatures, parameter "
"inventories, exceptions, and compatibility guidance belong in the separate "
"package Documentation."
msgstr ""
"DEAPack "
"是本书的计算配套工具，而不是组织全书的主角。每章先界定生产问题并推导理论测度，随后用代码重现某项论断，揭示得分背后的目标方案或分解，并检查解释该比较所需的条件是否成立。完整的函数签名、参数清单、异常说明和兼容性指南见单独的包文档。"

#: ../../preface.md:61 bcb1c3e0165d402fb3b3d468d0ae3ca0
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"This project extends earlier work on directional-distance efficiency and "
"green productivity software, including the Stata implementation by Wang, Du,"
" and Zhang {cite:p}`wang2022`. DEAPack broadens that computational setting "
"to classical DEA, productivity change, undesirable outputs, and structured "
"production systems. Its role here is to make the theory inspectable. A "
"reader can reproduce the numerical result, open the operating quantities "
"behind it, and see how a different orientation, scale assumption, direction,"
" or reference technology changes the conclusion."
msgstr ""
"本项目延续了方向性距离效率与绿色生产率软件方面的早期工作，其中包括 Wang、Du 与 Zhang 的 Stata 实现 "
"{cite:p}`wang2022`。DEAPack 将这一计算环境扩展到经典 "
"DEA、生产率变化、非合意产出和结构化生产系统。它在本书中的作用，是让理论可以被逐项检验。读者不仅能重现数值结果，还能查看结果背后的经营数量，并观察导向、规模假设、方向或参照技术的改变如何影响结论。"

#: ../../preface.md:69 ae91496eb4224836a61eb19856824158
msgid ""
"The book and its computational companion therefore use the same notation, "
"datasets, worked examples, and visual language. This continuity lets "
"equations, code, tables, and figures describe one empirical argument rather "
"than four disconnected versions of it. It also keeps the distinction between"
" a mathematically valid benchmark and a credible management conclusion "
"visible throughout the analysis."
msgstr "因此，本书与其计算配套工具采用同一套符号、数据集、完整案例和视觉语言。这样的连贯性使公式、代码、表格和图形共同讲述一条经验论证，而不是彼此割裂的四种版本；也使数学上有效的标杆与可信的管理结论之间的区别始终清晰可见。"

#: ../../preface.md:75 5a651d3334774ecaa62ee24ce30ed110
msgid "Reproducible evidence"
msgstr "可重复的证据"

#: ../../preface.md:77 5363b001ade34cf69838206d5ba85937
msgid ""
"Every numerical statement, table, and figure is expected to be reproducible "
"from the repository. Small theoretical datasets are deterministic and "
"isolate questions such as proportional resource saving, output shortfall, "
"unit invariance, infeasible historical comparisons, or productivity-index "
"circularity. Empirical datasets retain provenance, processing steps, "
"variable definitions, units, and version information. A result that cannot "
"be regenerated reliably will not be used as a teaching conclusion."
msgstr "本项目要求代码库中的每个数值陈述、表格和图形都可以重现。小型理论数据集采用确定性设计，分别揭示比例性资源节约、产出不足、单位不变性、不可行的历史期比较或生产率指数循环性等问题。经验数据集则保留来源、处理步骤、变量定义、单位和版本信息。无法可靠再现的结果不会作为教学结论。"

#: ../../preface.md:84 b81bcd28ba1e46919069b4ae95bcfe48
msgid ""
"The project is designed to provide open access to the manuscript, "
"computational examples, and every dataset whose redistribution rights have "
"been cleared. This allows readers to inspect how each conclusion was "
"obtained and to challenge the assumptions that produced it. Reproducibility "
"is not treated as proof that those assumptions are correct. It is a way to "
"separate numerical agreement from the harder questions of comparability, "
"measurement, economic interpretation, and external validity."
msgstr "本项目力求公开提供手稿、计算示例，以及所有已明确获得再分发许可的数据集。这使读者能够检查每项结论是如何得到的，并质疑产生该结论的假设。可重复性并不能证明这些假设正确；它的作用，是把数值一致性与可比性、测量、经济解释和外部有效性等更困难的问题区分开来。"

#: ../../preface.md:90 55831bb9fd9148da91ae18ce8503fb85
msgid "An open scholarly project"
msgstr "一项开放的学术工程"

#: ../../preface.md:92 4701ece96be24e7ebc1d92151860478c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The Handbook and DEAPack are developed in public. Readers may suggest a "
"model, identify an equivalence that should be made clearer, report a "
"numerical discrepancy, contribute code or a teaching case, improve a figure,"
" or refine the Chinese translation. A well-documented question or "
"counterexample is valuable even when the contributor does not implement a "
"solution. The {doc}`project-contributions` page explains the available "
"routes, the evidence expected for a new executable method, and how "
"contributions are credited."
msgstr ""
"Handbook 与 DEAPack "
"均以开放方式开发。读者可以建议模型，指出尚需澄清的等价关系，报告数值差异，贡献代码或教学案例，改进图形，或者润色中文译文。即使贡献者没有实现解决方案，一个记录充分的问题或反例也很有价值。{doc"
"}`project-contributions` 页面说明了参与途径、新增可执行方法所需的证据以及贡献致谢方式。"

#: ../../preface.md:99 9dda55b1d5e44df99390764f7f455fea
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr "预备知识"

#: ../../preface.md:101 dbfd31d134d64f5ea74d1c48c16fa098
msgid ""
"No previous course in linear programming or production economics is assumed."
" Each method begins with a production or management problem; the required "
"mathematics is introduced only after the reader knows what is being compared"
" and why. Figures help connect operating data, benchmarks, and decision "
"consequences. Familiarity with basic Python and pandas will make the "
"computational sections easier to reproduce, but the theoretical sequence can"
" be read independently of the code."
msgstr ""
"本书不要求读者预先修读线性规划或生产经济学。每种方法都从一个生产或管理问题出发；只有当读者明白比较什么、为何比较之后，才引入必要的数学。图形帮助读者把经营数据、标杆和决策后果联系起来。具备"
" Python 和 pandas 基础有助于重现计算部分，但理论主线也可以脱离代码独立阅读。"
